  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Given that $\u2016u\u2016=5$ and $u\\cdot v=-15$, find the smallest possible value of $\u2016v\u2016.$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le \u2016u\u2016\\cdot \u2016v\u2016 \\\\ |-15| & \\le 5\\cdot \u2016v\u2016 \\\\ 15 & \\le 5\\cdot \u2016v\u2016.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of the inequality by $\\frac{1}{5}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 15 & \\le \\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 5\\cdot \u2016v\u2016 \\\\ 3 & \\le \u2016v\u2016\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $\u2016v\u2016$\nis  $3.$",
